dracut-luks (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix bogus TPM2 PIN prompt at boot for tokens enrolled without a PIN.
    Enrolled LUKS2 tokens (systemd-tpm2 / systemd-fido2) are now detected
    at update-grub time and emitted as UUID-scoped rd.luks.options
    (tpm2-device=auto / fido2-device=auto), putting systemd-cryptsetup on
    its native token path; new crypttab entries carry the same options so
    dracut pulls the tpm2-tss/fido2 modules into the initramfs itself.
  * 20-luks-tokens.conf: gate on library files instead of dpkg package
    names (the t64 ABI rename made libtss2-esys undetectable on noble,
    leaving TPM support out of the initramfs), and require the tpm2
    binary before adding the tpm2-tss module (its check() hard-fails the
    initramfs build without tpm2-tools).
  * Recommend tpm2-tools; dracut-luks-setup --check now verifies the
    token chain (crypttab option, plugin in initrd, rd.luks.options in
    grub.cfg).

 -- Joshua Miller <freshroot@lamille.net>  Fri, 15 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0000

dracut-luks (0.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. GRUB drop-in that derives rd.luks.* at update-grub
    time, dracut drop-ins for the crypt modules and FIDO2/TPM2 token
    plugins, and the dracut-luks-setup helper.

 -- Joshua Miller <freshroot@lamille.net>  Fri, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
